    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d263-a1">

                <pb facs="0263" n="941" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg941"/>

                <head>Colonel Balluzeck to Mr.
                        Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Russia in China</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Peking</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 1, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister:</hi> I have the honor of announcing to
                    you that his Majesty the Emperor, my august master, having deigned to accord me
                    authority to return to Russia, I leave shortly my post of representative of his
                    Majesty in China, and that Mr. de Glinka, secretary of this legation, remains
                    chargé d’affaires of the Emperor at Peking until the arrival of my
                    successor.</p>
                <p>Permit me to express here the hope that your excellency will continue to accord
                    to Mr. Glinka the same warm regard that I have constantly received from you, and
                    to manifest the wish that you may be well persuaded that the remembrance of the
                    amicable relations which have not ceased to exist between us will always be
                    precious to me.</p>
                <p>I desire earnestly that our personal connexions, in losing their official
                    character, may not be entirely broken; and it is in this thought that I renew,
                    Mr. Minister, the expression of the very high consideration with which I have
                    the honor to be, of your excelleney, the very humble and very obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>L. D. BALLUZECK.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
